{"body":"Accept verified partial findings for 30005116 / OWR-10252930-028. The unrestricted induced-four-cycle profile problem remains **unsolved, 5/5**.\n\nThe packet proves the source construction's full profile for multipartite graphs and weighted cographs and their limits, a density-preserving replacement for specified complete joins, and a consequence for every asymptotic triangle-minimizing sequence using credited Pikhurko–Razborov stability. It also proves a precisely qualified small-amplitude local theorem, explicit nonmultipartite equality examples and L1-close tying paths, and the complete rank-one latent-product profile strictly below the achievable source construction at every interior density. None supplies the missing all-host comparison.\n\nAcceptance follows source-first root reconstruction, three independent reviews across distinct mechanisms, a new whole-package adversarial audit, and independent reproduction of complete stored outputs. All 93,505 author assertions and 1,080 historical review assertions replay exactly. Fresh independent universal proofs and controls supplement those finite checks. Five fresh pinned primary PDFs were read and revalidated separately; portable wrappers do not fetch sources. No novelty certification is claimed.\n\nOriginal head: c683fc4b84266a6a153c087e182cf427ed502d6c. Author checkpoint: e27668a5dd99e38705ec6a97d15710b7eb1b0f41. First queue-only refreshed head: 26df33899c95d860403ab311c568e0328bc87eeb, with parent ceada39994b1cd2c4935709143b53e2f7a581a45. After a persistent stale GitHub test-merge cache, the first normal expected-head update produced intermediate head 4afe89d1439e0d0d2a28a55f27709192cd56738e, with parents [26df33899c95d860403ab311c568e0328bc87eeb, 8e04757bff6e5c6c25d2dbf23ce10f736da8c5c8] and tree9b4c96e230fc3aecca24760e6804ea671d559ca4. Concurrent acceptance advanced main and its other queue rows. A second normal expected-head update merged current main eb3c6dbe6a1d978e39c30518137264bdc69ec30b into that reviewed head, producing final reviewed head 2bb07868e8fb5ac48cae8ec0b7f69aed02b36807, exact parents [4afe89d1439e0d0d2a28a55f27709192cd56738e, eb3c6dbe6a1d978e39c30518137264bdc69ec30b] and full tree 1464f6e71c9db2ab696db9e75373413267030156. All 45 original mathematical/review/publication files remain byte-identical throughout. Against the current-main parent only this problem's queue status and turn count change; every other current-main path and queue byte is preserved. Historical pending-review statements and initial certificates remain frozen history, with the accepted disposition and additive final-head verification recorded in the descending audit.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in deriving, checking and reviewing these findings. This is independent AI-assisted verification, not external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification. The unrestricted gap, prior results and external theorem dependencies are explicit. Merge only as a partial result: no preprint, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker row or release is produced for this unsolved problem.\n\nAudit artifacts: draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr374_30005116 on main.\n","headRefOid":"2bb07868e8fb5ac48cae8ec0b7f69aed02b36807","isDraft":false,"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","state":"OPEN"}
